  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR changes no behaviour. It adds a characterisation test and a decision file for #2739.\n\n- `crates/app/tests/tilt_basis0_edited_file.rs` (new, 261 lines): two tests.\n- `docs/decisions/2739-tilt-basis0-edited-file.md` (new): the decision, the facts, the manual repair and the dropped options.\n\n## Readings\n\nThe test uses the Tormach 770MX + microARC 4 (A only) and a slot drawn from (10,0) to (30,0) at A0 B180.\n\n- A tilt with `basis_version: 0` generates the slot along world Y at X0. Basis 1 generates it along world X at Y0. The cut plane turns 90 degrees about the tool axis.\n- The preview and the post agree. The basis-0 operation posts `G1 X0 Y-10` / `X0 Y-30`. A basis-1 operation drawn at (0,-10)..(0,-30) has the same world toolpath and posts the same G1 lines. Basis 1 at the drawn slot posts `X10 Y0` / `X30 Y0`.\n- No field in the file tells the edited file from a legal one. A legal pre-#2133 project with A0 B180 at basis 0 (the shape of the \"Flat A180\" operation in `crates/app/tests/fixtures/legacy-tilt-basis.camproj`) is the same file, byte for byte, as a project that a #2599 build saved after the edit A90 -> A0 B180. The file states no saving build and no edit history. Every build from project v65 to v72 had the defect (v0.24.0 included), and the fixed build also writes v72.\n\n## Decision\n\nNo safe load test exists. A warning on the edited file also fires on the legal \"Flat A180\" project, and the re-entry that the warning asks for moves a correct cut. Thus the load door changes nothing. The release notes carry the limit and the manual repair. This issue closes as a decided limit. The dropped options are in the decision file.\n\nThe facts do not show a gouge or a hidden plane: the post states the toolpath that the preview shows.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `tilt_basis0_edited_file::a_basis0_a0_b180_file_posts_the_turned_plane_that_its_preview_shows`\n- `tilt_basis0_edited_file::an_edited_basis0_file_is_the_same_file_as_a_legal_unedited_one`\n\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`) on 89e3d7c0d: 1 step, 0 failed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test tilt_basis0_edited_file -- -D warnings`: clean. `tilt_basis_compat` and `first_4axis_part` are not changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A real file from v0.24.0 or an older build: the test makes the file state with a JSON edit of a saved project.\n- Machines other than the microARC 4, and other angles where basis 0 and basis 1 differ.\n- The stock simulation and the collision verifier on such a file.\n- The GUI.\n\nChangelog: Known limit (#2739): a project that a build before this release saved after a change of a tilt angle on an operation from a project file older than version 65 (no tilt basis key) can keep the old plane basis. Such an operation cuts the plane turned 90 degrees from a new operation at the same angles (for example A0 B180), as the preview shows. To repair it, change Tool axis A or B to a different value, set it back, and check the preview before you post.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2739\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
